Z||000000||Elenor84||02-08-2001||06:28 PM||||Hey guys, is the throttle cable that is being sold at fiero store going to solve my stiff pedal?  Is that all I need?<BR>thx!<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||danny boy||02-08-2001||06:46 PM|||| It should. When I got my GT the rear manifold cracked and was spraying(for lack of a better term)hot exaust directly on the throttle cable. It had melted the outside to the inside. I put a new cable on and it was fixed. the only thing that can stick is the cable.||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnnyK||02-08-2001||07:18 PM||||I thought it was the only that could stick too, but upon removing the throttle cable from the engine, I could move the cable/pedal assembly easily by hand (from the engine).. I just lubed everything in the engine and pedal assembly real good.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Elenor84||02-08-2001||11:30 PM||||And one more thing on my gas pedal...is this the same with all fiero's or only mine...u can press it down to a certain point and then it kinda stops...but then if u push real hard it moves to the floor...is the the cable to?<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Wannabe||02-09-2001||12:25 AM||||Just make sure it comes back  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Wannabe (edited 02-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||JohnnyK||02-09-2001||12:49 AM||||Disconnect it at the engine and take it from there.. That way if the pedal/cable assembly moves, it's the actual mechanical throttle linkage.||||reg||1
Z||000006||LZeitgeist||02-09-2001||08:33 AM||||If it's a V-6, chances are that it's actually not your cable that's sticky, it's the choke plate in the plenum... it's such a snug fit that *any* light amount of buildup in there will cause the plate to catch slightly, making the pedal feel as though it's stuck, and requiring extra pressure to free it. (This would be if the pedal feels stuck after you take your foot off the pedal.)<P>Take the intake hose off the plenum and spray some carb cleaner (make sure you use the stuff designed for fuel-injected engines!) in the plenum and move the choke plate around... wipe it out with a rag, and see if the pedal isn't sticky-feeling anymore. Once the plate is moving freely again, reinstall the intake hose and remember how you did it for next time... I've had to do this about every three months to keep mine from sticking slightly. I'm not sure if it's the humidity down here (in North Carolina) or what, but it's annoying cleaning it out so often. <P>If it's a 4-cyl., then please ignore the above advice.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>(note - edited for typos... I hate those things!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)<p>[This message has been edited by LZeitgeist (edited 02-09-2001).]||||reg||1
